Paninda revision 003 — Google Drive / Sheets integration
Date: 2026-11-05 (UTC)
Branch: litmus_2
Base: litmus_1 at 1de1a71

REQUEST
Implement real Google OAuth, workbook connection/disconnection, modular local-first
Sheets translation, Settings conflict suggestions and Figma 28:404 warning/error
layout. Compatibility detection is deferred; the notice must be blanket and
rephrased. Keep clean startup and the lean regression suite.

IMPLEMENTED
- Removed the production local-session onboarding bypass. Home opens only after
  Google authorization, workbook initialization/read and local binding succeed.
- Google Play services AuthorizationClient handles account/permission resolution,
  token renewal requests and grant revocation. No client secret, service account,
  refresh token or Google access token is persisted in Room or logged.
- Native Drive listing is scoped to app-authorized, app-marked Paninda workbooks.
  Uses drive.file, OpenID and email scopes instead of whole-Drive access.
- Create a separate Paninda Workbench spreadsheet file with six canonical tabs;
  write original row-1 headers at A1 and read back before recording a connection.
  Mark reconnectable only after initialization verifies. No sample data added.
- Reconnect to existing accessible Paninda workbooks, bound by account subject ID
  and workbook ID. Different nonempty local data is not silently replaced.
- Modular Google HTTP/Drive/Sheets adapters translate the shared ShopSnapshot
  through the existing schema/mapper; core business models remain provider-free.
- Manual local-first synchronization uses a common baseline and canonical hashes.
  Upload local-only changes, import remote-only changes, acknowledge identical
  copies, stop on divergence. Recheck remote before upload and verify afterward.
- Room imports/acknowledgements compare the captured local hash transactionally.
  Changes made during network work retain their pending entries. Verified receipt
  records are acknowledged; incomplete/ambiguous uploads do not clear the outbox.
- Real disconnect revokes Google's app grant before returning to onboarding.
  Preserve local records/outbox, remote workbook and the prior comparison binding.
  Revocation failure is shown; offline disconnection is not falsely reported.
- Local reset invalidates the sync baseline. An empty device can restore remote
  data; reset must never upload an empty snapshot as a remote deletion.
- Settings displays account, workbook, sync state and contextual conflict/contract
  guidance. Sync/disconnect/reset controls block overlapping cloud operations.
- Figma warning/error page: supplied gradient and serif hero, independently
  scrolling body, fixed Start Over / Proceed or Try Again actions. New workbook
  selection page follows existing fonts/palette/Material icons.
- Blanket warning explicitly says compatibility detection is pending, rather than
  claiming incompatible rows were detected. Existing-workbook schema validation
  still guards import/write integrity. Failed setup retry discards selection and
  restarts Google authorization; normal sync retry obtains authorization and reads
  both copies again.
- Updated per-page string resources, current prototype/schema documentation and
  Google Cloud/device acceptance guide. Existing Room schema version stays 1:
  connection state uses its existing key/value table. Backup/transfer excludes
  app data to avoid restoring stale workbook bindings onto another device.

CLOUD SETUP REQUIRED BY PROJECT OWNER
Enable Google Drive API and Google Sheets API. Configure OAuth branding/audience,
Data Access and tester accounts. Register an Android OAuth client:
  package: com.paninda.app
  current workspace debug signing SHA-1:
  E3:CC:05:81:10:48:DA:34:32:9C:33:BE:DA:E4:7F:33:46:21:07:48
A differently signed APK needs a matching registration. No Web client ID, API key,
client secret or google-services.json is required by this native authorization
flow. See docs/GOOGLE_SHEETS_SETUP.md for steps and official references.

LIMITATIONS / PENDING
- General-purpose compatibility detection and adoption of arbitrary existing
  spreadsheets remain deferred. Required schema validation is already enforced.
- Native selection is NOT a full Google Drive picker. Full Google Picker / other
  spreadsheets / Excel import are not implemented.
- SINGLE WRITER ONLY: Sheets batchUpdate has no compare-and-swap here. Before/
  after reads narrow but cannot eliminate the concurrent-editor overwrite window.
  Do not edit Sheets or another device during sync. Reliable concurrent writes
  need a coordinator/versioned write protocol, not just snapshot comparisons.
- Manual sync only. No background worker, polling, automatic mutation retries,
  automatic merge, row-diff UI, force overwrite or local-only backup export.
- An interrupted creation/upload may already have reached Google. Orphaned or
  duplicate workbook files can remain; the app does not silently delete files.
- Real Google authorization/revocation/API acceptance needs a configured Cloud
  project and physical Play-services device. No account/device validation is
  claimed from the local regression suite.
- Reports, selling/checkout, vendor-management tools, stock counts/receiving,
  adjustments, staff roles and other financial workflows remain pending.
- Google logo remains the requested placeholder; Custom Database remains locked.

VERIFICATION
- All 13 focused maintained checks passed: the prior 10 plus three sync data-loss
  regressions. Covers divergence/second-read edits, in-flight local edits,
  ambiguous upload retry and safe remote restoration after a local reset.
- No maintained layout tests, screenshot baselines or device-size matrix added.
  A temporary render harness stays under ignored work/ solely for inspection.
- Final APK / lint / visual inspection results are appended below after checks.

FINAL CHECKS
- Final assembleDebug + lintDebug succeeded. Android lint: 0 errors; remaining
  warnings are dependency-version notices and optional toUri/KTX style advice.
- Inspected one-off warning, failure and compact large-text renders. Gradient
  hero matches Figma 28:404; messages scroll separately and bottom actions remain
  accessible. The render harness/images are ignored scratch files, not a suite.
- Debug APK: app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk. Signing fingerprint checked
  against the Cloud setup guide. No APK upload or remote Git push requested in
  this implementation turn.
